    {
      "title": "Germany’s far-right AfD thanks Elon Musk as France warns state election win a ‘serious moment’",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/07/afd-thanks-elon-musk-german-state-elections-2026-win",
      "description": "<p>Lead candidate in Saxony-Anhalt welcomes further ‘strong’ cooperation with Musk as French minister says ‘We cannot forget our history’</p><p>The candidate who led the far-right Alternative für Deutschland party to a historic state election victory in Germany has thanked Elon Musk for his support, as one French minister warned that this was a “serious moment” for Europe.</p><p>The AfD more than <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/06/saxony-anhalt-germany-afd-exit-poll-ulrich-siegmund\">doubled its support in the Saxony-Anhalt region</a> and appears to be on the brink of becoming the first far-right party to gain power in Germany at state level since the second world war.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/07/afd-thanks-elon-musk-german-state-elections-2026-win\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-07T01:03:39"
    },
    {
      "title": "Far-right AfD wins key German state election but may fail to secure majority",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/06/saxony-anhalt-germany-afd-exit-poll-ulrich-siegmund",
      "description": "<p>Projections show Alternative für Deutschland on 44.4% of vote in Saxony-Anhalt after huge turnout, with votes still being counted</p><p>The populist, far-right, anti-immigration Alternative für Deutschland (AfD) has emerged as the winner in a crucial state election in Germany, exit polls have projected, securing a historic result and more than doubling its support. The AfD now appear on the brink of becoming the first far-right party to gain power in Germany at state level since the second world war.<strong> </strong></p><p>Initial exit polls showed the party to have secured 44.4% of the vote, a larger share than predicted, and<strong> </strong>decisively larger than that of the Christian Democrats (CDU) of the chancellor, Friedrich Merz, in a contest that was being followed across the world. However, it still remains unclear as to how and whether the AfD will be able to form a government, having ruled out entering a coalition and being refused any form of cooperation by the mainstream parties<strong>.</strong></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/06/saxony-anhalt-germany-afd-exit-poll-ulrich-siegmund\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-06T18:13:29"
    },
